            <h2>Route Overview: Alexandria to Roanoke</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Alexandria to Roanoke by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect Northern Virginia with the heart of Virginia's Blue Ridge Mountains. This route provides passengers with a relaxed alternative to driving or flying especially popular for leisure travelers, outdoor enthusiasts, students, and weekend trips. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the Northeast Regional offers comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and spectacular views through Virginia's historic Piedmont and mountainous regions.</p>
            <p>The route is served by Amtrak's Northeast Regional, offering daily departures between Alexandria Union Station and Roanoke's downtown station. Compared to road travel on I-81 and I-64, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic and mountain driving stress, delivering you straight into downtown Roanoke without worrying about parking or rental cars. The Northeast Regional connects Roanoke to the broader Northeast Corridor, making it easy to reach destinations like Washington, D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York, and Boston. </p>
